25,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
26,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The fixed costs are quite high, and the usage is heavily skewed toward weekends and holidays.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems that checking figures creates resentment, and the constant need to ask favors is what sours these groups.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It is worse than I thought. Weekly trips are collapsing, and the car is often returned dirty or empty.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shion,,The fuel spending is incredibly lopsided. A few of us are paying for almost everything while others contribute nothing.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,Recording every run takes a lot of time—nearly an hour a week—and the diary shows huge gaps in usage.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, if the fuel is that uneven, a simple split isn't fair. We need a way to track actual use.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,But @Daisuke just mentioned that tracking is time-consuming. We must avoid a system that creates more work and resentment.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Exactly. If we just track distance, who ensures the car is clean and fueled for the next person?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shion,,"We can't ignore the financial imbalance. Someone is subsidizing the others, which is logically unsound.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I don't want to spend my evenings calculating fuel costs or arguing about who forgot to clean the car.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Minako,,We need a balance between precision and peace. A fixed system might reduce the need for constant negotiation.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A fixed system removes the ""favor"" aspect, which the other households mentioned as a primary point of failure.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"As long as my weekly needs are guaranteed and the car is ready, I am open to suggestions.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shion,,"A fixed share is simple, but it doesn't solve the issue of those who drive significantly more.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just want something that doesn't require a meeting every time I need to go to the store.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Minako,,It seems we are torn between absolute fairness and operational simplicity.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. The goal is to stop the ""clipped replies"" and return to a harmonious household.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Asuka,,Let's see the options and decide based on these findings.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shion,,Agreed. Let's move to the voting.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,Okay.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
